<title>USA: ABB among top US bear-market picks -- report.</title>
<headline>ABB among top US bear-market picks -- report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asea Brown Boveri AB's low price risk and good earnings growth should enable its stock to hold its value in the event of a U.S. bear market, according to a portfolio manager in Barron's weekly.</p>
<p>Steven Lehman at First National Bank of Chicago also listed Washington Post Co, Amoco Corp, Tecumseh Products Co, and MAPCO Inc among his top 10 bear-market picks in the newspaper's September 9 issue.</p>
<p>The manager's list also included McCormick and Co Inc, Freeport-McMoRan Inc, Reader's Digest Association Inc, Rubbermaid Inc, and Public Storage Inc.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
